            <div xml:id="d668">

                <pb facs="0753" n="660" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg660"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">638.5131/57: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chapin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-04T13:00:00-05:00">June 4, 1935—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>45. My telegram No. 42, May 29, 1 p.m.<anchor n="41" xml:id="d668-f1"/> On
                    instructions of Haitian Government, Fiscal Representative today informed
                    customhouses that French imports no longer come under most-favored-nation
                    treatment and will be subject to maximum tariff, that is, 100 per cent surcharge
                    on former regular tariff.</p>
                <p>Goods on high seas as of May 27 exempted.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chapin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
